  "body": "\"If the attribute is specified and there is an element in the tree whose ID is equal to the value of the for attribute\" \r\nNothing there hints that the attribute shouldn't work when elements aren't in document.\r\nAlso, how should this all work when elements are in shadow DOM or in document fragments.\r\n\r\nI assume ID refs shouldn't work when not in document, but should work when in document, or in shadow dom or in document fragment.\r\n\r\nThe behavior of .labels when element isn't in document isn't too clear either.",
